--- stdout
Build a Spago package to Go and run it, or with --js run it with Node.js.

Usage: googoo run [FLAGS] [-- ARGUMENTS]…

Arguments:
  [-- ARGUMENTS]…  Arguments passed to the program.

Flags:
  -p, --package <NAME>       Workspace package to build.
  -o, --output <DIR>         Output directory. Defaults to output in the workspace root.
  -q, --quiet                Suppress build progress and Spago output.
      --color <COLOR>        When to use colors in diagnostics and progress output.
                             [possible values: auto, always, never]
                             (default: auto)
      --main <MODULE>        Module containing the program entry point.
      --js                   Run with Node.js instead of compiling to Go.
      --go                   Compile to Go and run the executable, which is what `run` does anyway. Needs Go 1.27 or
                             later.
      --entry <MODULE.NAME>  Qualified entry point, such as Main.main. Defaults to main in --main's module.
      --pgo <PROFILE>        Optimise the executable for this CPU profile (go build -pgo), or `off` to leave out the one
                             --profile recorded.
      --profile              Run the program once while recording a CPU profile, keep it in .spago/go/<package>/
                             default.pgo and build again optimised for it. Later builds use it until --pgo off.
  -h, --help                 Print help
--- stderr
